{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the men came upon the women.</b> That is, to take their ornaments from them, as it is written: ״חח ונזם״, and even so the women were joyful and zealous for the heavenly labor, as it is written: ״כל הנשים אשר נשא לבן אותנה״. Therefore the women merited not to do work on Rosh Chodesh, because in the episode of the calf their ornaments were taken from them against their will, as is implied by what is written: ״ויתפרקו״ etc., whereas in the episode of the Mishkan they rejoiced in giving. Therefore He gave them Rosh Chodesh as a Yom Tov. And it appears to me that this is Rosh Chodesh Nisan, in which the Mishkan was erected, and along with that Rosh Chodesh, all the Rosh Chodesh days of the entire year were likewise established."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:45.471660653Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}